         TITLE     'BITS'
         SUBTITLE  'The bit functions of Cray FORTRAN, as functions'
         IDENT     BITS
         COMMENT   'BITS - AND, OR, XOR, NOT, IAND, ISHFT'
*
*  Cray Blitz calls the Boolean functions of Cray FORTRAN several hundred
*  thousand times a second.  The kit's compiler does not know them, so
*  they are functions here, in assembly language to make the calls as
*  short as they can be.  A function finds the addresses of its arguments
*  at 0,A7 and 1,A7 and returns its value in S7.
*
TEXT     SECTION   CODE

         ENTRY     @AND
         ENTRY     @IAND
@AND     BSS       0
@IAND    BSS       0
         A1        0,A7
         A2        1,A7
         S1        ,A1
         S2        ,A2
         S7        S1&S2
         J         B00

         ENTRY     @OR
@OR      BSS       0
         A1        0,A7
         A2        1,A7
         S1        ,A1
         S2        ,A2
         S7        S1!S2
         J         B00

         ENTRY     @XOR
@XOR     BSS       0
         A1        0,A7
         A2        1,A7
         S1        ,A1
         S2        ,A2
         S7        S1\S2
         J         B00

         ENTRY     @NOT
@NOT     BSS       0
         A1        0,A7
         S1        ,A1
         S7        #S1
         J         B00
*
*  ISHFT(I, N): I shifted left N places, or right -N places when N is
*  negative, with zeros brought in.  A count of 64 or more gives zero.
*
         ENTRY     @ISHFT
@ISHFT   BSS       0
         A1        0,A7
         A2        1,A7
         S7        ,A1
         S1        ,A2
         S0        S1
         JSM       ISHFTR
         A1        S1
         S7        S7<A1
         J         B00
ISHFTR   BSS       0
         S1        -S1
         A1        S1
         S7        S7>A1
         J         B00

         SECTION   *

         END
